        "answer": {
          "short": "$ST=aL$. Correct answer: C.",
          "worked": "At the intersections of $y=x^2$ and $y=k$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2&=k\\\\x&=\\pm\\sqrt{k}\\\\L&=\\sqrt{k}-(-\\sqrt{k})\\\\L&=2\\sqrt{k}\\end{align*}$$\n\nAt the intersections of $y=\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}$ and $y=k$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2}{a^2}&=k\\\\x^2&=a^2k\\\\x&=\\pm a\\sqrt{k}\\\\ST&=a\\sqrt{k}-(-a\\sqrt{k})\\\\ST&=2a\\sqrt{k}\\\\ST&=aL\\end{align*}$$\n\nHere $a>0$, so $\\sqrt{a^2}=a$.\n\nCorrect answer: C.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
